text.section:
Any locality establishing a tourism improvement district may enact ordinances on any of the following subjects that provide for:

Activities and other additional services required for tourism promotion or events or for enhancement of the tourism improvement district;


Activities in the tourism improvement district that will fund the promotion of tourism activities in the tourism improvement district, including acquiring, constructing, installing, or maintaining capital improvements;


Operating and maintaining any tourism improvement district activity;


The charging of fees on all benefited businesses within a tourism improvement district, which shall be charged on the basis of the estimated benefit to such businesses within the tourism improvement district;


The classifying of businesses for purposes of determining the benefit to the businesses of the activities provided pursuant to this article;


A process for the collection of revenues from fees from benefited businesses; and


Forming a tourism improvement district in cooperation with, and that includes, other localities.
